💝 GRATITUDE TO THE LINEAGE
To Buddha (2,500 years ago):
For showing that suffering has structure, that liberation is possible through awareness, that we're not separate
selves but processes in flux. You gave me the soil everything grows from.
To Freud, Lacan, Žižek:
For making the unconscious speak, for showing symptoms have meaning, for connecting inner world to
ideology. You taught me to look beneath surface.
To Klein, Bowlby, Winnicott:
For human warmth, for hope in relationship, for showing repair is possible. You gave me relief after abstraction,
even though I eventually needed more.
To Saussure, Peirce, Foucault, Bourdieu:
For showing how meaning is made, how power operates through discourse, how habitus shapes us. You
connected language, power, and position.

To Jung, Myers-Briggs:
For normalizing my cognitive difference, for INFJ language, for showing patterns without pathology. You
helped me understand how I process reality.
To Ivan Illich (my birthday twin):
For protecting dignity, for critiquing institutions, for conviviality. You died so I could be born, and your
questions live in my work. He he.
To Meadows, Bateson, Forrester, Luhmann:
For systems thinking, for ecology of mind, for feedback and complexity. You showed me patterns across scales,
mind as systemic.
To von Foerster, Bateson (again), Glanville:
For cybernetics, for including observer, for ethics explicit. You bridged everything and made design for values
possible.
To Whitehead, Bergson, Deleuze:
For process over substance, for becoming over being, for relational ontology. You gave philosophical
foundation for what I already intuited.
To Buber, Levinas, Butler, Haraway:
For I-Thou, for infinite responsibility, for precarity, for situated knowledge. You gave me ethical heart, the core
of the framework.
To Varela, Thompson, Maturana:
For enactivism, for bringing forth world through action, for integrating Buddhism and cognitive science. You
bridged my root and Western science.
To Prigogine, Kauffman:
For dissipative structures, for self-organization, for showing thermodynamic necessity of asymmetry. You gave
physics foundation for everything.
To Wallerstein, Fanon, Said, Spivak, Chakrabarty, Nandy:
For world-systems analysis, for postcolonial critique, for epistemic violence, for epistemologies of the South.
You helped me understand my positioning as Sri Lankan in Global South.
To Deepthi Kumara Gunaratne:
For making psychoanalysis real in Sri Lankan context, for showing local appropriation of global theory is

possible. You're the homegrown flame.
To all the thinkers not listed but present in spirit:
You shaped this too, even if not explicitly named. The conversation is larger than any map can capture.
To YOU (reading this, me, future self):
For following the questions wherever they led. For not giving up when paralyzed. For building this on your
birthday. For claiming your right to create philosophy from your position. For continuing the conversation.
You're not just inheritor of lineage. You're lineage-maker yourself now.

